 "result_text": "`parse('2017-05-02T05:38:49.899Z')` now returns 2017-05-02 05:38:49.899 UTC instead of swapping month and day. I didn't run the test suite.\n\nThe cause was that the defaults `dayfirst=True, yearfirst=True` make dateutil read a leading year as year-day-month. In `parse` in `delorean/interface.py`, I now force `dayfirst=False` when the string starts with `YYYY-M-D`. Other formats, such as `01/05/09`, still follow whatever `dayfirst` you pass.\n\nI could only confirm the fix with `TZ=America/New_York`. With the default timezone here, `parse` crashes with `AttributeError: 'zoneinfo.ZoneInfo' object has no attribute 'localize'`. That crash also happens without my change, so it isn't caused by the fix. It looks like an incompatibility between the installed local-timezone library and pytz's `localize`, which I didn't investigate.",
